{{Term/Store|Sunshroom|Sunshrooms|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC, AoI|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="AoC Material"/><ref name="AoI Materials"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Sunshroom}}
Sunshrooms are a type of [[Mushroom]] that can found growing near [[Tree]]s in [[Eldin Canyon]] and the [[Gerudo Highlands]]. They can be purchased from [[The Slippery Falcon]] and [[Ardin]]'s [[Stall]] in [[Gerudo Town]]. They can be eaten as is to restore half a [[Heart]] to [[Link]]'s [[Life Gauge]], but they can also be [[Cooking|Cooked]] into [[Food]] to restore greater health and provide [[Cold Resistance]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> When Sunshrooms are burned by [[Fire]], they become [[Toasty Sunshroom]]s. In addition, Sunshrooms can be used as an ingredient at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]] to create [[Dye|Red Dye]].

After Link upgrades his [[Sheikah Sensor]] at the [[Hateno Ancient Tech Lab]], [[Symin]] will ask to see it.<ref name="BotW Symin"/> When Link speaks to Symin next, he decides to demonstrate how he can use Sheikah Sensor to find [[Item]]s that are depicted in the [[Hyrule Compendium]].<ref name="BotW Symin 2"/> He tasks Link with taking a Picture of a Sunshroom, pointing out that one can be found behind the Lab.<ref name="BotW Symin 3"/> This begins the "[[Sunshroom Sensing]]" [[Side Quest]].

Once Link returns with a Picture of a Sunshroom, Symin will ask to see it to confirm.<ref name="BotW Symin 4"/> He is pleased to see the Picture, and he then tasks Link to tune his Sheikah Sensor to his Hyrule Compendium Picture of the Sunshroom.<ref name="BotW Symin 5"/> He then asks Link to bring him three Sunshrooms using the Sheikah Sensor.<ref name="BotW Symin 6"/> After gathering three Sunshrooms, Link can return to Symin and hand them over.<ref name="BotW Symin 7"/> When Link does so, Symin thanks Link and gives him three [[Hearty Truffle]]s as a reward.<ref name="BotW Symin 8"/>

Another Side Quest, "[[Riddles of Hyrule]]," involves [[Walton]] telling Link riddles and having him bring the corresponding Item. For his third riddle, Walton will ask Link to find a Mushroom that warms one's bones and can be found in warmer areas.<ref name="BotW Walton"/> If Link places a Sunshroom on the leaf in front of Walton, he will cheer that Link figured out the riddle.<ref name="BotW Walton 2"/>

